   "evidence": "`Bicategory.Equivalence` and `mkOfAdjointifyCounit` are defined in Mathlib's `Bicategory/Adjunction/Basic.lean`, the file's first import. `symm`/`trans` use only that API (`mkOfAdjointifyCounit`, `whiskerLeftIso`, `\u03b1_`, `\u03bb_`) and never mention pseudofunctors.",
   "file": "TauCeti/CategoryTheory/Bicategory/Biequivalence.lean",
   "fix": "Move the `Equivalence` section to `TauCeti/CategoryTheory/Bicategory/Adjunction/Basic.lean`, mirroring Mathlib's `Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Bicategory.Adjunction.Basic`, with only that import. `Biequivalence.lean` then imports that file (or only `FunctorBicategory.Pseudo`) and keeps just the `Biequivalence` structure.",
   "issue": "`Equivalence.symm`, `Equivalence.trans` and their `_hom`/`_inv` simp lemmas are general operations on adjoint equivalences in any bicategory. Nothing about biequivalences or pseudofunctors is involved, yet they live in `Biequivalence.lean`, which also imports `FunctorBicategory.Pseudo`. Users looking for the inverse or composite of a `Bicategory.Equivalence` will not find them under that name.",
   "line": 43
  }
